.TH "LINTO-COMMANDS" 1

.SH "Command usage"
.PP
The \fBlinto\fP dispatcher locates commands relative to this checkout, so you can
run them from any current working directory\. Common forms are:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto \-\-help                         # active groups and commands
linto GROUP                          # show a guide page, then list group commands
linto GROUP COMMAND [ARGUMENTS\.\.\.]   # explicitly select a group
linto COMMAND [ARGUMENTS\.\.\.]         # use a unique command name
linto\-GROUP\-COMMAND [ARGUMENTS\.\.\.]   # generated group\-qualified stub
.fi
.RE
.PP
When enabled by the group's \fBshort\-stubs\fP setting, unique commands also have a
\fBlinto\-COMMAND\fP stub\. A command's own help is generally available through
\fBlinto COMMAND \-\-help\fP or \fBlinto help GROUP COMMAND\fP\.
.PP
\fBlinto help\fP displays the guide index\. Use \fBlinto help PAGE\fP to read a guide
topic, or \fBlinto help page PAGE\fP when the topic name is also an active group
name\. For example, \fBbibtex\fP is both a guide topic and a group, so use
\fBlinto help page bibtex\fP to select its guide page\. The group listing takes
precedence for \fBlinto help GROUP\fP\.
.PP
The dispatcher also supports \fBslug\fP as an alias for \fBstripaccents\fP\. Run
\fBlinto \-\-list\-groups\fP to list active groups and \fBlinto \-\-list\-commands GROUP\fP
to list a group's commands\.

.SS "Shell aliases"
.PP
\fBlinto launch aliases\fP installs or updates aliases declared in
\fBlaunch/lib/aliases\.yml\fP for one shell\. For example:
.RS
.PP
.nf
aliases:
  zz: "linto launch zed"
unaliases:
  \- old\-alias
.fi
.RE
.PP
By default, the command detects the shell from \fB$SHELL\fP, then tries the parent
process, and falls back to \fBsh\fP if it cannot identify one\. Select a shell
explicitly with \fB\-s\fP or \fB\-\-shell\fP:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto launch aliases \-\-shell fish
linto launch aliases \-s bash
.fi
.RE
.PP
Choices are \fBfish\fP, \fBzsh\fP, \fBbash\fP, \fBsh\fP, and \fBksh\fP\. Fish aliases are saved with
Fish's \fBalias \-\-save\fP mechanism\. For Bash, Zsh, sh, and ksh, Linto replaces the
managed alias block in \fB~/\.bashrc\fP, \fB~/\.zshrc\fP, \fB~/\.profile\fP, or \fB~/\.kshrc\fP,
respectively\. Names listed in \fBunaliases\fP are omitted from the managed aliases;
for Fish, Linto also erases the saved alias function\. Start a new shell or reload
your shell's configuration for the changes to take effect\.
